;
; TEXTURE AUDIT (mandatory per asset-import-pipeline.md and this task's brief — the
; DeadTree/PineTree2 precedent): probed every surface's albedo_texture/albedo_color/
; vertex_color_use_as_albedo on the raw, unmodified FBX import (same throwaway-script
; method used to diagnose those two bugs). Result: albedo_texture is null on every
; surface (this pack, like its own OBJ/MTL sibling export, never shipped map_Kd texture
; references at all — confirmed by inspecting Barn.mtl directly), BUT
; vertex_color_use_as_albedo reads true with MEANINGFUL, DISTINCT per-surface colors
; (e.g. surface 0 ~ dark red (0.4872, 0.228, 0.1966), surface 1 ~ light grey trim
; (0.821, 0.821, 0.821), surface 2 ~ mid red-brown (0.5601, 0.2625, 0.2265), surface 3 ~
; dark grey/roof (0.311, 0.311, 0.311)) — NOT the uniform near-(0.9063, 0.9063, 0.9063,
; 1.0) tell that flagged DeadTree/PineTree2 as broken. This pack bakes each of its named
; flat-color Blender materials (DarkRed/LightRed/RoofBlack/White etc., see Barn.mtl) into
; real per-vertex color at FBX export time, the same genuinely-vertex-colored shape
; BirchTree/Bush already established elsewhere in this project. No texture fix needed; no
; material_override applied. Plain instance, matching House.tscn's convention exactly.
;
; SCALE: raw AABB measured via manual local-transform composition on the unmodified FBX
; (NOT global_transform — see cultivated_field.tres's header for why that silently
; returns identity on a freshly-instantiated, not-yet-tree-attached node; same method
; Task 2 used for the House variants): footprint 7.7269 x 8.2224 (x, z) tile-units,
; height 6.0086. Barn is this task's proposed 2x2-footprint outlier (FLAG FOR HUMAN
; SIGN-OFF, see barn.tres's header) — target max-axis is therefore 2x House's own
; established 1x1 margin (0.869309), i.e. 1.738618, not the 1x1 target every other farm
; building in this batch uses. Long axis (z) scaled by 0.211448 to hit that target.
; Scaled result: 1.6338 x 1.2705 x 1.7386 (x, y, z) — fits inside a 2x2 tile footprint
; with the same "small margin, not edge-to-edge" fit House's own variants used.
